          "path": "_m/g/c/w/2/bridgewater-hall-wp/manchester-rochdale-canal-88-4.jpg",
          "filename": "Manchester Rochdale Canal 88 4594.JPG",
          "caption": "The Rochdale Canal in Manchester built in 1800, passes between the Ashton Canal in Piccadilly and the Bridgewater Canal at Castlefield. The 'Rochdale Nine' locks are 84:Dale St, 85:Piccadilly, 86:Chorlton St, 87:Lock 87, 88:Lock 88, 89:Tib, 90:Albion Mills, 91:Tunnel, 92:Duke's. This section never closed. The junction with Manchester and Salford Junction Canal between ,88 ,89. opened in 1839 and closed in 1922.\nSwing Bridge at Manchester and Salford Junction Canal basin.\n\n\nCamera location53° 28′ 27.48″ N, 2° 14′ 43.08″ W View this and other nearby images on: OpenStreetMap 53.474300;   -2.245300",
          "alt": "The Rochdale Canal in Manchester built in 1800, passes between the Ashton Canal in Piccadilly and the Bridgewater Canal at Castlefield. The 'Rochdale Nine' locks are 84:Dale St, 85:Piccadilly, 86:Chorlton St, 87:Lock 87, 88:Lock 88, 89:Tib, 90:Albion Mills, 91:Tunnel, 92:Duke's. This section never closed. The junction with Manchester and Salford Junction Canal between ,88 ,89. opened in 1839 and closed in 1922.\nSwing Bridge at Manchester and Salford Junction Canal basin.\n\n\nCamera location53° 28′ 27.48″ N, 2° 14′ 43.08″ W View this and other nearby images on: OpenStreetMap 53.474300;   -2.245300",
          "width": 1280,
